    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0225" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg211"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/179</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United Kingdom Representative to the
                        European Advisory Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Strang</hi>)<anchor n="52" xml:id="d111-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">E.A.C. (44) 17</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-02">2 May, 1944</date>.<anchor n="53"
                            xml:id="d111-f2"/>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Machinery in Germany During the “Middle Period”,
                        i.e. the Period of Military Government After Hostilities Cease</hi>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>On 22nd March, 1944 I circulated to the Commission a paper (E.A.C. (44)
                        14) covering a memorandum outlining the structure of the machinery of
                        control through which the proposed High Commission would work during the
                        period when the High Commission would be the Supreme Allied authority in
                        Germany.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I explained that that memorandum did not deal with the organization of the
                        machinery of control required in the “middle period”, that is to say the
                        period between the cessation of hostilities and the opening of the period
                        when the High Commission would be the Supreme <pb facs="0226" n="212"
                            xml:id="pg212"/> Allied authority in Germany. I said that the United
                        Kingdom Delegation hoped in due course to submit a further memorandum for
                        the “middle period” also.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I now circulate to the Commission, as an Annex to the present paper, a
                        memorandum making proposals for the machinery of control required for
                        Germany during the “middle period”, that is to say, the period of military
                        government after the cessation of hostilities.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">illiam</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >trang</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d111-a1.xml" xpointer="d111-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d111-f1" n="52" type="source" xml:id="d111-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in the United Kingdom in his
                    despatch 15413, May 4; received May 13.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d111-f2" n="53" xml:id="d111-f2-content">
                <p>The memorandum was originally circulated in the European Advisory Commission by
                    the United Kingdom Representative on May 1.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
